<Context>
	<!-- SSR-1 (AUDIT_FINDINGS.md): upstream ships Lax here, which silently
	     breaks session continuity the moment this app is loaded inside a
	     cross-origin iframe, exactly how mod_tutorship embeds an OM room
	     inside Moodle (different host/port = third-party context to the
	     browser). A Lax cookie set on the iframe's own first request is
	     never sent back on that same iframe's later requests (only "safe"
	     top-level navigations qualify for Lax), so every subsequent request
	     lands in a brand-new session with no soap/hash state, observed
	     directly as WebSession.checkHashes() firing twice for one hash, the
	     second call finding it "already used" and rejecting a session that
	     had, moments earlier, genuinely authorized.

	     None is correct ONLY for an HTTPS-fronted deployment (the shape
	     staging/production actually run): the None SameSite attribute is
	     valid ONLY in combination with Secure, and Tomcat's own
	     Rfc6265CookieProcessor adds Secure only when the triggering request
	     was itself HTTPS (verified: HTTP gets no Secure, HTTPS gets Secure).

	     CORRECTION (2026-09-14, SSR-2): an earlier version of this comment
	     claimed None was a harmless "no-op" over plain HTTP because "Chrome
	     discards a None cookie lacking Secure and falls back to its own
	     default." That is FALSE and was the root cause of a hard breakage on
	     local HTTP dev: a browser does not fall back to a default; it
	     REJECTS a SameSite=None cookie that lacks Secure outright, storing
	     nothing. Over plain HTTP (local dev on :5080) Tomcat emits
	     "JSESSIONID=...; HttpOnly; SameSite=None" with no Secure, the browser
	     drops it, JSESSIONID is never returned, every request creates a fresh
	     servlet session (visible as a churning ;jsessionid= URL rewrite and
	     checkHashes seeing "has soap in session ? false" each time), the
	     room's stateful WebSocket can never persist, room.js's
	     /websocket/closed handler fires _reload(), and the room enters an
	     endless ROOM_ENTER/ROOM_LEAVE page-reload loop, and no video ever
	     renders. (allowSameURLMultipleTimes only stopped the hash itself
	     being rejected on the re-entry; it did not fix the session loss.)

	     The value therefore genuinely depends on the deployment's transport
	     and cannot be a single hardcoded constant for a single image used
	     across both HTTP and HTTPS. It is left as None here (the correct
	     default for the HTTPS iframe-embed case that motivated SSR-1), but is
	     overridable at container start: set OM_SAMESITE_COOKIES=Lax for a
	     plain-HTTP deployment and om.sh rewrites this attribute before Tomcat
	     starts (see docker/scripts/om.sh). Lax keeps top-level room entry
	     working over HTTP; cross-origin iframe embedding fundamentally cannot
	     work over plain HTTP regardless (the browser forbids a cross-site
	     cookie without Secure), so no value recovers that case for HTTP. -->
	<CookieProcessor sameSiteCookies="None" />
</Context>
